19297,13.5,1956,38,99,26],[19298,23.5,1956,48,91,24]],"links":[["Santa Fe County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/new-mexico/santa-fe-county"],["ARC or PLC in Santa Fe County","/arc-plc/new-mexico/santa-fe-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, from 1951 to 2025. May to June came in under 90% of normal in 40 of those years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 15 grids, the most of any pair. In 2025 the middle saw January to February at 29% and May to June at 252%, and so far in 2026 February to March sits at 25%. Every grid had its driest year in 1956, with grid 18696 at 34%.</p>"}
